Patterns should unfold neatly. Pattern calculation follows sequence rules. Base case: 1 has 1 pattern. For n > 1: f(n) = sequence(n) + append pattern of f(n-1). A seemingly crude approach simplifies beautifully. Use recursion for this, since pattern shaping depends on n-1 patterns.
